11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark is a 2019 supernatural horror film directed by André
Øvredal, based on the book series of the same name by Alvin Schwartz.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The screenplay was adapted by the Hageman Brothers, from a screen story by Guillermo del
Toro (who also produced), as well as Patrick Melton and Marcus Dunstan.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The film, an international co-production of the United States and Canada, stars Zoe Colletti, Michael Garza, Gabriel
Rush, Austin Zajur, Natalie Ganzhorn, Austin Abrams, Dean Norris, Gil Bellows, and Lorraine Toussaint.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
In 2013, CBS Films acquired the rights to the book series from 1212
Entertainment, with the intent of producing it as a feature film.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
By January 2016, it was announced that del Toro would develop
and potentially direct the project for CBS Films.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Øvredal was later set to direct the film, with del Toro,
Daniel, Brown, and Grave being among the producers.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
Principal photography began on August 27, 2018, and
ended on November 1, 2018, in St.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
Thomas, Ontario, Canada.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark was theatrically released on
August 9, 2019, in the United States by Lionsgate Films.

20
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The film was well received by critics with praise for its depictions of the horror features from its source
material, and went on to gross $105 million at the box office, becoming a financial success.

21
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
A sequel is in development.

